# Releases

* Format: "LANGUAGE VERSION"

## Janet 0.1.0

### Added

* A Janet implementation of NRDL, in `janet/`, with the parser expressed as a
  PEG grammar following the ABNF in the README, using Janet's built-in `peg`
  module. `parse-from` accepts the same `:json-keys-as-keywords` keyword
  argument as the Common Lisp implementation, so JSON documents can be parsed
  into tables with keyword keys.
* `generate-to` with `:pretty-indent` and `:json-mode` options, mirroring the
  Common Lisp implementation. Since Janet tables cannot hold `nil`, parsed
  nulls arrive as the `:null` keyword (the convention used by `spork/json`).
* Tests in `janet/tests`, run via `jpm test`.

## CL 0.8.0

### Added

* Added a `:json-keys-as-keywords` keyword argument to `parse-from`, and an
  exported `*json-keys-as-keywords*` special variable it binds. When true,
  string keys found in maps are interned as keywords (via `string-symbol`)
  during deserialization, so JSON documents can be parsed into maps with
  keyword keys.
* Added tests around this.

## CL 0.4.0

### Added

* Added an export, `*symbol-package*`, a parameter that controls into which
  package the symbols will be interned when NRDL is parsed.
* Added a test around this

### Changed

* Renamed package to `com.djhaskin.nrdl`
* Renamed system to `com.djhaskin.nrdl`
* Migrated from `rove` to `parachute` for tests
* Reduced the dependencies in the ASD list.
